{#
mail/_send_outcome.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What the browser is told once the send has actually happened.

Rendered by App\Service\Mail\SendOutcomeNotifier in the WORKER, published over
Mercure, and applied by core--mercure. Rendered rather than described because
the alternative is building a toast in JavaScript, which means a second copy of
_toast.html.twig that drifts from the first.

WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL

"Message sent." used to be said by ComposeController::sent(), which the browser
calls when the cancel window closes — at eight seconds. The send is held for
ten. So the confirmation preceded the attempt by two seconds, every time, for
everybody, and a send that then failed was never mentioned again.

Variables: message, sent (bool)

A failure is worded by its reason (#125), read off the row the handler has just
marked: "may have been sent" and "the server refused it" ask different things of
the reader. Failed — the reason with nothing more to say — keeps the old words.
#}
{% set failure = sent ? null : message.sendFailure %}
{% set failedKey = failure and failure.value != 'failed' ? 'toast.send_failed_' ~ failure.value : 'toast.send_failed' %}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            type:    sent ? 'success' : 'error',
            message: sent
                ? 'toast.sent'|trans
                : failedKey|trans({ '%subject%': message.subject|default('')|slice(0, 60) }),
            extra:   sent ? {} : { hide_after: 12000 },
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

{# The message itself, where the conversation showed it as being sent.

   A message built in the browser has nothing to show while the send job holds
   it — the body was sealed or blanked, and the raw source is the bytes that
   go out — so mail/_message_body.html.twig says it is being sent instead
   (`data-sending-sealed`). Nothing else ever revisited that: the
   conversation is not re-rendered in the background, so a reply to encrypted
   mail sat there "being sent" until the page was reloaded, long after it had
   gone. This is the moment the page can be told.

   `targets` with :has(), so only a message that is on screen AND still says
   it is being sent is swapped: a plain reply, already showing its body, is
   left alone, and a page without the conversation matches nothing. The frame
   loads the message in the person's own request (ComposeController::
   settledRow()), because opening it needs the keyring and the session this
   worker does not have. A refused send comes back as the draft it is again. #}
<turbo-stream action="replace" targets="#thread_message_{{ message.id }}:has([data-sending-sealed])">
    <template>
        <turbo-frame id="settled_message_{{ message.id }}" src="{{ path('app_compose_settled_row', { id: message.id }) }}"></turbo-frame>
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
